  The entitlements set of the pfp executable: EMPTY, by design (SECURITY.md §12,
  ADR-003). No JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no library-validation bypass,
  no debugging entitlement, no sandbox exception, nothing.

  This file exists so that the empty set is written down and tested: `cargo
  xtask` fails its tests if a key ever appears in the dictionary below. The
  release pipeline does NOT pass it to codesign (no entitlements option on the
  codesign command line and this empty dictionary mean the same thing); if the keychain spike of
  PLAN.md §4.1 ever finds an entitlement to be necessary, that is an ADR first
  and an edit here second.
-->
